hostap-s1g (2.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian/rules: enable 802.11s mesh support (CONFIG_MESH) in
    wpa_supplicant_s1g.
  * debian/rules: enable the PEAP, MD5, MSCHAPv2, TLS (including TLS 1.3),
    TTLS, GTC and PWD EAP methods in wpa_supplicant_s1g so it can join
    WPA-Enterprise (802.1X) networks.
  * debian/rules: stop appending CONFIG_IEEE80211AH, CONFIG_S1G_TWT,
    CONFIG_MORSE_STANDBY_MODE and CONFIG_MORSE_KEEP_ALIVE_OFFLOAD to the
    wpa_supplicant configuration; the upstream defconfig already enables
    them.

 -- Austin <vidplace7@gmail.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

hostap-s1g (2.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release (upstream tag mm8108-2.1.0).
  * debian/watch: track the per-chip 'mm8108-' tags; upstream now tags the
    MM6108 and MM8108 series separately, so the stale note about upstream
    having no tags is dropped.
  * debian/watch: match the archive extension in filenamemangle so the
    downloaded tarball is not named hostap-s1g-<version>.tar.gz.tar.gz.
  * debian/rules: fetch the 'mm8108-<upstream version>' tag in
    get-orig-source, derived from the changelog version.
  * debian/copyright: extend Morse Micro copyright years to 2026.

